Fix xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland leaking one file descriptor per
zwp_linux_dmabuf_feedback_v1.format_table event.

The format_table event transfers ownership of the fd to the client. The
handler in CPortalManager mmap()s it and then returns without ever closing
it -- on any of its three paths:

  * the `if (dma.done) return;` early-out never touches the fd at all;
  * the MAP_FAILED branch returns after the failed mmap;
  * the success path falls off the end.

mmap() takes its own reference to the underlying file, so the fd should be
closed immediately after mapping; keeping it open buys nothing and holds the
descriptor for the lifetime of the portal.

This is not a one-shot: the compositor re-sends format_table whenever the
feedback changes (an output being added or removed, a GPU change), so a
long-running session accumulates descriptors. The `dma.done` early-out makes
the post-initialisation case strictly worse -- those events leak the fd
without even remapping the table.

Found while auditing fd lifetimes in this codebase after an unrelated,
much larger leak in the input-capture portal. This one is slow and does not
strand in-flight AF_UNIX fds, so it does not produce the ETOOMANYREFS failure
mode that motivated the audit -- but it is a plain descriptor leak on a path
that fires on ordinary monitor hotplug.

Not upstreamed yet.

diff --git a/src/core/PortalManager.cpp b/src/core/PortalManager.cpp
index 5dc98d4..3ee23c9 100644
--- a/src/core/PortalManager.cpp
+++ b/src/core/PortalManager.cpp
@@ -152,12 +152,21 @@ void CPortalManager::onGlobal(uint32_t name, const char* interface, uint32_t ver
         m_sWaylandConnection.linuxDmabufFeedback->setFormatTable([this](CCZwpLinuxDmabufFeedbackV1* r, int fd, uint32_t size) {
             Debug::log(TRACE, "[core] dmabufFeedbackFormatTable");
 
-            if (m_sWaylandConnection.dma.done)
+            // The format_table event transfers ownership of the fd to us, and
+            // mmap() takes its own reference to the underlying file, so the fd
+            // must be closed on EVERY path -- including the early-outs, which
+            // otherwise leak one fd per event for the lifetime of the process.
+            // This is not a one-shot: the compositor re-sends format_table
+            // whenever the feedback changes, e.g. on an output or GPU change.
+            if (m_sWaylandConnection.dma.done) {
+                close(fd);
                 return;
+            }
 
             m_vDMABUFMods.clear();
 
             m_sWaylandConnection.dma.formatTable = mmap(NULL, size, PROT_READ, MAP_PRIVATE, fd, 0);
+            close(fd);
 
             if (m_sWaylandConnection.dma.formatTable == MAP_FAILED) {
                 Debug::log(ERR, "[core] format table failed to mmap");
